PERF-01/02/05 found the event loop stalling on O(sheet-size) hot paths
and a synchronous fsync; behind the fsync fix sits the worker pool
D37 already specified but never built. The owner asked whether the
pool belongs in claudia-core so all three apps could share it;
reading cli.py showed the premise was wrong — make_plan() starts one
Hub per OS process for exactly one --model, so there is no single
running process hosting all three apps to share a pool across in the
first place. Records the corrected decision: the pool lives in
claudia-server, and each server process owns its own instance.

